# Process hygiene: never kill by size

A large process is not a safe one to kill. Before proposing to kill anything, answer what is lost if it dies half-way, confirm the pid is still the same one, and identify a session's leftovers by `ppid == 1`, never by name. Invoke `orphan-process-cleanup` when memory is short, when a failure looks like a resource problem, or before reaping anything.
